# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Text2SQL — Environment Configuration
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# Copy this to .env and set your values.
# Each TEXT2SQL_ variable maps to a flat Settings field (see src/text2sql/config.py).
# Env vars override YAML values. Sections follow the pipeline in execution order and
# mirror configs/config.yaml, which nests them (sql_generation.agent.max_turns → the
# flat TEXT2SQL_AGENT_MAX_TURNS below).
#
# Unknown TEXT2SQL_ vars are silently ignored — a typo here fails quietly, so keep
# names in sync with Settings.


# ── General ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TEXT2SQL_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
# Log every message sent to the model and every reply, tool calls included
TEXT2SQL_LOG_TRANSCRIPT=false
# Stop the pipeline early: "" | profiling | schema_linking | sql_generation
TEXT2SQL_STOP_AFTER=


# ── LiteLLM ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider API keys (LiteLLM reads these automatically, set only what you need):
# https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers/
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
GEMINI_API_KEY=...
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...
FIREWORKS_AI_API_KEY=...
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=...
# For local models (Ollama), no key needed — just set the model below.
# OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434 or http://host.docker.internal:11434 if using Docker on Mac/Windows
OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://host.docker.internal:11434

TEXT2SQL_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
TEXT2SQL_TEMPERATURE=0.0
TEXT2SQL_LLM_RETRIES=3
TEXT2SQL_LLM_IDLE_MS=1000
# none | low | medium | high. Extended thinking and sampling are coupled: anything but
# `none` forces temperature=1, which Anthropic requires while thinking is on.
TEXT2SQL_REASONING_EFFORT=none

# ── AWS Bedrock (LLM account) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Credentials for the AWS account that hosts Bedrock, routed to LiteLLM.
# TEXT2SQL_BEDROCK_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# TEXT2SQL_BEDROCK_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# TEXT2SQL_BEDROCK_AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=      # temporary STS creds only
# TEXT2SQL_BEDROCK_AWS_REGION=us-east-1


# ── SQLAlchemy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TEXT2SQL_DB_URI=sqlite:///example.db
# TEXT2SQL_DB_URI=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/mydb
# TEXT2SQL_DB_URI=mysql+pymysql://user:pass@localhost:3306/mydb
# TEXT2SQL_DB_URI=awsathena+rest://athena.us-east-1.amazonaws.com:443/mydb

# ── AWS Athena (database account) ────────────────────────────────────
# Credentials for the AWS account that hosts Athena, routed to pyathena's
# connect_args. Only applied when TEXT2SQL_DB_URI is an awsathena:// URI.
# TEXT2SQL_ATHENA_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# TEXT2SQL_ATHENA_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# TEXT2SQL_ATHENA_AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=       # temporary STS creds only
# TEXT2SQL_ATHENA_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# TEXT2SQL_ATHENA_S3_STAGING_DIR=s3://my-athena-results-bucket/staging/


# ── Profiling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local directory or s3://bucket/prefix for cached profiles.
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_CACHE_DIR=.cache/profiles
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_TOP_K=10
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_SAMPLE_SIZE=10000
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_ONE_CALL_PER_TABLE=true   # true = 1 LLM call per table; false = 1 per column
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_EXACT_TOP_K=true          # true = exact per-column GROUP BY top-k; false = from sample
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_APPROX_DISTINCT=false     # dialect approx distinct-count where supported; exact elsewhere
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_SAMPLE_AGGREGATES=false   # false = exact full scan; true = aggregate over a LIMIT-n sample
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_SUMMARY=short_and_long    # short | long | short_and_long
TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_KB=true                   # derive cross-column relations (1 LLM call per table)
# TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_SELECTION has no env form (nested dict) — set it via YAML or the UI.


# ── Schema Linking ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
TEXT2SQL_USE_SCHEMA_LINKING=true
# Which linkers run, unioned. A list-valued setting is parsed as JSON.
TEXT2SQL_SCHEMA_LINKING_MODES=["value"]
# Direct — read only when 'direct' is selected. schema_scope x descriptions = one prompt each.
TEXT2SQL_DIRECT_SCHEMA_SCOPE=["full"]          # full (whole DB) | focused (fields the question points at)
TEXT2SQL_DIRECT_DESCRIPTIONS=["short"]         # short | long generated column descriptions
TEXT2SQL_DIRECT_KNOWLEDGE=full                # off | terms | full (adds each term's definition)
# Reversed — read only when 'reversed' is selected.
TEXT2SQL_REVERSED_SCHEMA_SCOPE=["full"]
TEXT2SQL_REVERSED_DESCRIPTIONS=["short"]
TEXT2SQL_REVERSED_KNOWLEDGE=full
# Candidate ranking — feeds 'value' mode and any 'focused' schema scope.
TEXT2SQL_VALUE_TOP_K=30                        # floor under the candidate budget, which is 45% of the schema

# ── SQL Generation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
TEXT2SQL_GENERATION_MODE=direct              # direct = single-shot prompting | agent = ReAct tool loop
TEXT2SQL_NUM_CANDIDATES=1                     # 1-3; above 1 requires GENERATION_STRATEGY=diverse
TEXT2SQL_GENERATION_STRATEGY=direct          # direct | decompose | query_plan | diverse
TEXT2SQL_GENERATION_KNOWLEDGE=full           # off | terms | full — domain terms in the prompt
# TEXT2SQL_PROMPT_TEMPLATE_DIR=src/text2sql/prompts/templates
# TEXT2SQL_PROMPT_VERSION=v1
# Per-prompt overrides, read by PromptManager directly (not Settings fields):
# TEXT2SQL_PROMPT_GENERATE_SQL_PATH=/path/to/custom_generate.j2
# TEXT2SQL_PROMPT_REPAIR_SQL_PATH=/path/to/custom_repair.j2

# Agent — read only when TEXT2SQL_GENERATION_MODE=agent.
TEXT2SQL_AGENT_MAX_TURNS=12
TEXT2SQL_AGENT_MODE=exec                    # exec | full (adds checker + lookup tools) | retrieval (table names only)
# TEXT2SQL_SCENARIOS_FILE=scenarios.md     # needs AGENT_MODE=full or retrieval


# ── Verification ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Post-generation checking and candidate choice. Selection needs NUM_CANDIDATES > 1.
TEXT2SQL_USE_REPAIR=true
TEXT2SQL_MAX_REPAIR_RETRIES=2
TEXT2SQL_SELECTION_MODE=single             # single | majority | confidence


# ── Streaming ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TEXT2SQL_EVENT_VERBOSITY=verbose


# ── Benchmark ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated id prefixes; empty runs every instance
TEXT2SQL_BENCHMARK_INSTANCE_ID=
TEXT2SQL_BENCHMARK_OUTPUT_DIR=results/
TEXT2SQL_BENCHMARK_DATA_JSONL=/app/data/livesqlbench_data_sqlite.jsonl
# Reference SQL and test cases are withheld by the benchmark authors to prevent data
# leakage, and are not redistributed here. Request them from bird.bench25@gmail.com,
# then point this at your copy. Any filename starting with local_ is git-ignored.
TEXT2SQL_BENCHMARK_TESTCASES_JSONL=data/local_livesqlbench_sqlite_gt_kg_testcases_20260601.jsonl
TEXT2SQL_BENCHMARK_DATASET_FOLDER=/app/data
TEXT2SQL_BENCHMARK_USE_KNOWLEDGE=true


# ── AWS (only for Lambda/S3 deployment) ──────────────────────────────
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
# TEXT2SQL_PROFILE_CACHE_DIR=s3://my-bucket/profiles
